WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.780 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
When the market moves, one number rarely tells the

00:00:02.780 --> 00:00:05.860 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
whole story. Buffer gives you a clearer view of

00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:07.920 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
how your perpetual positions fit together.

00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:11.240 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
Start with a portfolio you can edit, or read

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:12.540 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
a public Solana account.

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:15.660 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
Change the price move and follow each long and

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:18.300 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
short, with the math and its assumptions close at

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:22.660 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
hand. For eligible Velocity accounts, current maintenance headroom

00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:24.900 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
sits beside a separate liquidation estimate.

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:28.640 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
The source and observation time remain visible, so you

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:29.760 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
know what you're looking at.

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:33.640 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
Monitoring brings headroom and market distance into the same

00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:38.060 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
workspace. Destination readiness and delivery status stay distinct.

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:41.780 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
A saved report keeps the explanation, not just the

00:00:41.780 --> 00:00:45.820 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
headline number. Velocity and Pacifica support price scenarios.

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:48.300 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
Jupiter adds position inventory.

00:00:49.220 --> 00:00:52.000 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
Across desktop and mobile, Buffer gives you room to

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:54.000 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
understand your exposure before you act.

00:00:54.820 --> 00:00:55.840 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
A little more perspective.
